id: pm-context-resume-recovery-sha
title: Resume must consume a verified same-version changelog recovery
description: "The release decision selects the oldest untagged Release pm-context v commit and records its immutable SHA. Verify merged release checks out that SHA before Restore prepared release notes reads CHANGELOG.md. A later notes-only repair on main cannot repair the historical commit, so dispatch still refuses. Define and verify an explicitly authorized same-version recovery revision without weakening artifact, metadata, ancestry or gate checks. No dispatch or workflow mutation is part of the notes repair."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-29T18:26:13.491Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T21:09:56.658Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T21:09:56.658Z",claude-hub,"Fixed in release.yml 'Restore prepared release notes': when the prepared commit has no section for NPM_VERSION, the step extracts the same-version section from origin/main (fetched and ancestry-verified by 'Verify merged release'), prints a notice, and still fails closed when neither has it. New test 'resume notes fall back to the same-version section of merged main when the prepared commit lacks it' builds a real git history (prepared commit without the section, later main commit with it, detached checkout) and also asserts a version absent everywhere refuses with empty RELEASE_NOTES.md. Revert proof: with the previous step the new test fails, with the fix it passes; release-workflow.test.ts 15/15. After this PR merges, dispatch release.yml to resume v2026.10.29."
files[1]{path,scope}:
  .github/workflows/release.yml,project
tests[1]{command,scope,timeout_seconds,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
  node --test --test-name-pattern='resume notes' test/release-workflow.test.ts,project,300,claude-hub,"2026-10-29T21:09:55.299Z",local_mutation,fix/changelog-2026-10-29
body: ""
